.TH REDBRUTE 1 "November 2026" "REDBRUTE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redbrute \- Python-based web authentication testing tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redbrute
.B -u
.I URL
.B -m
.I FAIL_MESSAGE
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B REDBRUTE
is a Python-based web authentication testing tool designed for efficient and resource-conscious wordlist processing in authorized security testing environments.

It uses batch-based wordlist loading to reduce memory consumption by processing a configurable number of entries at a time rather than loading an entire wordlist into memory.

REDBRUTE also supports concurrent HTTP request execution, allowing multiple requests to be processed simultaneously.

The tool provides configurable request methods, custom wordlists, HTTP headers, cookies, proxies, request timeouts, batch sizes, and worker threads.
.SH REQUEST METHODS
REDBRUTE supports the following HTTP request methods:
.TP
.B gu
GET URL. Used when the authentication parameter is included in the URL query string. Requires
.BR --param .
.TP
.B gf
GET Form. Used for GET-based form authentication. Requires
.BR --auth-param .
.TP
.B pf
POST Form. Used for POST-based form authentication. Requires
.B --data
and
.BR --param .
.PP
Select the appropriate method according to the target application's authentication mechanism. Missing or incorrect parameters may result in invalid requests.
.SH REQUIRED OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -u ", " --url " " URL
Specify the target URL.
.TP
.BR -m ", " --fail-message " " MESSAGE
Specify the response message that indicates a failed authentication attempt.
.SH OPTIONAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --wordlist " " FILE
Specify a custom wordlist. Defaults to
.B ./rockyou.txt
when omitted.
.TP
.B --data " " DATA
Specify the HTTP request data. Required for the POST Form method.
.TP
.B --param " " PARAMETER
Specify the parameter being tested. Required for GET URL and POST Form methods.
.TP
.B --auth-param " " PARAMETER
Specify the authentication parameter for the GET Form method.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BR -k ", " --verify
Disable SSL certificate verification.
.TP
.B --cookie " " COOKIE
Specify HTTP cookies.
.TP
.B --header " " HEADER
Specify custom HTTP headers.
.TP
.B --proxy " " URL
Specify a proxy URL for request debugging and interception.
.TP
.B --timeout " " SECONDS
Specify the HTTP request timeout in seconds. Default: 4.
.TP
.B --batch-size " " SIZE
Specify the number of words loaded into memory per batch. Default: 1000.
.TP
.B --thread-counts " " COUNT
Specify the number of concurrent worker threads. Default: 100.
.TP
.B --method " " METHOD
Specify the HTTP request method. Accepted values:
.BR gu ", " gf ", " pf ", " get-url ", " get-form ", " post_form .
Default: pf.
.SH WORDLIST PROCESSING
REDBRUTE includes a default wordlist named
.B rockyou.txt
containing over 14 million password entries in commonly distributed versions.

A custom wordlist can be supplied using
.BR --wordlist .
If no custom wordlist is specified, the included wordlist is used.

REDBRUTE processes wordlists incrementally using configurable batches. This avoids loading the entire wordlist into memory and helps reduce memory consumption.
.SH PERFORMANCE
The default configuration uses a batch size of 1000 words and 100 worker threads.

Users should adjust these settings according to available system resources and the authorized testing environment.

For live-site testing, a conservative thread count below 20 is recommended, subject to the site's rate limits and testing authorization.

On systems with limited RAM or CPU resources, reducing the batch size below 1000 may help improve resource management.

Higher thread counts and larger batches do not necessarily guarantee better performance.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B Basic execution
.nf
redbrute -u http://127.0.0.1/login -m "Login failed"
.fi
.TP
.B Specify a custom wordlist
.nf
redbrute -u http://127.0.0.1/login -m "Login failed" \\
    --wordlist passwords.txt
.fi
.TP
.B Configure batch size and threads
.nf
redbrute -u http://127.0.0.1/login -m "Login failed" \\
    --batch-size 500 --thread-counts 10
.fi
.TP
.B GET URL method
.nf
redbrute -u http://127.0.0.1/login -m "Login failed" \\
    --method gu --param username
.fi
.TP
.B GET Form method
.nf
redbrute -u http://127.0.0.1/login -m "Login failed" \\
    --method gf --auth-param username
.fi
.TP
.B POST Form method
.nf
redbrute -u http://127.0.0.1/login -m "Login failed" \\
    --method pf --data "username=admin&password=FUZZ" \\
    --param password
.fi
.TP
.B Use a proxy
.nf
redbrute -u http://127.0.0.1/login -m "Login failed" \\
    --proxy http://127.0.0.1:8080
.fi
.TP
.B Display help
.nf
redbrute --help
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./rockyou.txt
Default wordlist included with REDBRUTE.
.TP
.I ./assets/
Contains banner assets.
.TP
.I ./architecture/
Contains architecture documentation.
.TP
.I ./screenshots/
Contains project screenshots.
.SH AUTHOR
REDBRUTE Development Team.
